 "answer": {
  "answer": "The goal was not met: only one challenging setting was confirmed, on scene 023b7fcc. There, recorded cars shifted 1.5 s earlier at 1.25x speed made the policy fail on every repeat (S4). All failures in the study came from that scene and from the -1.5 s shift, at speed scales 0.5x, 1.0x and 1.25x (S2, S3, S4). Only S4 has enough repeats to put its failure rate surely above one half. S2 and S3 rest on one or two runs each, so they are hints, not rates. None of the other eight scenes failed in any run. Three of them were repeated enough to look safe at their most critical setting (S18, S19, S29). Triage put every failure on the policy and flagged no simulator artifacts. In most of them the ego drifted left off its route, even though the route command was RIGHT, and hit or scraped the cars beside or ahead of it (actors 13 and 56).",
